{
  "name": "chests",
  "about": "A town's stock shown in its desk's and depot's chests, at the end of each look that counted them: the stack its master Merchant puts on its own shop's shelf is moved out of the desk's chests, and books delivered to the town are moved into the chests' free slots, the desk's first. What didn't fit (a hopper filled the slot first) comes back as Unmoved and waits on the town's books until a count shows room. A desk broken takes its chests' goods with it, and put back where it stood is the same town, its chests counted in once. Saved and loaded, the chests are as the core took them.",
